WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:02.017 --> 00:00:06.017
Okay, so I’m here today at Bristol. 

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:08.017
My love affair with Bristol started in 2018, 

00:00:08.017 --> 00:00:12.517
and it’s been a very beautiful relationship since. 

00:00:12.517 --> 00:00:16.017
I’ve been to Bristol several times over the last six years.

00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:18.600
And one of the things that I love about Bristol is that the work it’s done 

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.017
over the last six years has been hugely influential. 

00:00:21.017 --> 00:00:25.017
Not only in the space of intersectionality, broadly speaking, 

00:00:25.017 --> 00:00:27.017
and race, specifically speaking, 

00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:30.517
it’s been a really great exemplar for other institutions in the locality

00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:33.017
and further on in the sector

00:00:33.017 --> 00:00:37.017
in terms of the amazing work they’ve done in areas like decolonising the curriculum,

00:00:37.517 --> 00:00:42.017
thinking about better employment interventions for black and ethnic minority staff,

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.517
looking at its promotion and progressions, 

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:47.034
thinking about how it diversifies its student body and staff body. 

00:00:47.034 --> 00:00:50.034
So there’s been some really good interventions that have happened 

00:00:50.034 --> 00:00:53.017
and also staff becoming more literate around 

00:00:53.017 --> 00:00:56.517
Black history and Black British history in particular

00:00:56.517 --> 00:00:58.517
So being part of some of those interventions over the last couple of years 

00:00:58.517 --> 00:01:00.517
and working with the ED and I team 

00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:05.517
and working with kind of academics of the like at Bristol has been hugely influential.  

00:01:05.517 --> 00:01:10.017
And yeah I think this is the 15th or 16th time I’ve been here in six years.  

00:01:10.017 --> 00:01:12.017
It really, really means a lot.

00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:14.017
So thank you so much for having me here today. 

00:01:14.017 --> 00:01:15.517
And yeah, it’s a blast. I love this place.

00:01:15.517 --> 00:01:17.017
My home away from home. 

00:01:17.017 --> 00:01:22.517
And yeah, I probably at some point I probably should have worked here at some point during my career. 

00:01:22.517 --> 00:01:26.017
I’ve been here that many times, but it might happen one day. 

00:01:26.017 --> 00:01:27.017
So thank you so much. 

00:01:27.017 --> 00:01:29.517
Really appreciate being here today.

